---
kind: scene
id: ines.balloon
title: The radiosonde
on: visit
target: place.deck
priority: 15
after: 'visited("ines.forecast")'
# Tried again every afternoon until the balloon is up (a torn balloon is a
# retry, not a spent scene).
spentBy: "run.balloonUp"
when: "run.slot == 'afternoon' && run.day <= 6"
---

## The balloon shed

::bg{location="deck" time="afternoon"}
::use{component="enter" who="ines" side="left" instance="use-001"}
@ines{code="0010" emotion="neutral"}: Radiosonde. Hydrogen, latex, a box of instruments the weight of a sandwich. It goes up twenty kilometres and tells us what the sky is doing where we can't see.
@ines{code="0020" emotion="worried" when="run.balloonTries > 0"}: {{run.balloonTries:plural(One balloon|# balloons)}} in the bin already. The Met Office bills us for them.
::set{run.balloonTries += 1}

<branch id="launch" prompt="The balloon strains at its cord like a dog that has seen a cat.">
  <choice id="now" label="Let it go now">
    <match on="run.weather">
      <when is="clear">
        ::set{run.balloonUp = true}
        @narrator{code="0010"}: It goes straight up, shrinking to a pearl, then a point, then nothing. The receiver in the radio room starts clicking.
        @ines{code="0030" emotion="happy"}: That's a launch. Write the time. To the second.
      </when>
      <otherwise>
        @narrator{code="0020"}: A gust takes it sideways into the mast. The pop is almost polite.
        @ines{code="0040" emotion="tired"}: Tomorrow. Wind and latex don't negotiate.
      </otherwise>
    </match>
  </choice>
  <choice id="wait" label="Wait for a lull">
    @ines{code="0050"}: Sensible. The lull doesn't come. Tomorrow, then.
  </choice>
</branch>
